    "dotnet-conventions": {
      "status": "local",
      "note": "Merged from the C#/.NET guides of client-endorsement-system-rewrite and myhealth-integration-layer; baseline for new .NET projects. Generalized from MyHealth findings: modular solutions, 422 validation variant, default-only error format, always-split slices, messaging-framework outbox. Names Wolverine-style generated code as a forced public surface. Error flow: unresolved body references are field Validation; handler-side field failures use ThrowError; FastEndpoints ToProblem builds on ProblemDetails (one formatter for validators, results, exception handler, status pages); downstream outcomes map to 502/503/504. Audited against .NET 10, FastEndpoints 8.3, xUnit v3 4.0, and Wolverine 6: added Dapper, Wolverine, and Blazor references (from client-endorsement-system, myhealth-integration-layer, emedcore-plus-integrations, and client-endorsement-system-rewrite); CA1852/CA2016 enforced in the editorconfig baseline; framework-generated 400s routed through ToProblem; BackgroundService exit-code note version-qualified for .NET 11."
    },
